# Cloudflare Pages headers. Vite copies everything in public/ to the build
# output root, so this ends up as build/_headers.
#
# Pages applies EVERY matching rule and joins duplicate header names with a
# comma. Cache-Control therefore appears on /assets/* only — repeating it under
# /* would produce "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, public, max-age=..."
# instead of overriding it.
#
# HTML needs no explicit rule: Pages already serves it as
# "Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate", so a new deploy is picked
# up on the next request.
#
# HSTS is deliberately absent — enable it once per zone under
# SSL/TLS > Edge Certificates > HSTS, otherwise Cloudflare's own header and this
# one get joined into an invalid value.
#
# The CSP below is looser than it would otherwise be, to host the Java Memory
# game (see the blog post). CheerpJ's runtime dynamically imports a blob URL and
# instantiates WebAssembly, so script-src needs `blob:` and `'wasm-unsafe-eval'`
# on top of its origin. This cannot be scoped to just the game's path: browsers
# enforce multiple CSP headers as an intersection, so a second, looser rule
# would not lift the strict one. `'wasm-unsafe-eval'` permits WebAssembly
# compilation only — it does not enable eval() for JavaScript.
#
# frame-ancestors and X-Frame-Options allow same-origin framing because the blog
# post embeds the game in an iframe. They were 'none'/DENY, which blocks framing
# even from the same origin.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob: https://cjrtnc.leaningtech.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://api.github.com https://cjrtnc.leaningtech.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Vite emits content-hashed filenames here, so these are safe to cache forever.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
